WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.187
So what changes?

2
00:00:01.187 --> 00:00:04.750
These are two different models,
not two versions of one product.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:10.438
Active Directory is a hierarchy:
a forest, domains, and nested OUs.

4
00:00:10.438 --> 00:00:12.291
Entra ID is one flat tenant,

5
00:00:12.291 --> 00:00:16.925
where structure comes from
attributes and administrative units.

6
00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:20.350
In AD, much of who you are is
where you sit in the tree.

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.936
In Entra ID, it should come
from attributes supplied by an

8
00:00:23.936 --> 00:00:27.598
authoritative source, and for
the workforce that means HR.

9
00:00:27.598 --> 00:00:31.718
Policy moves from Group Policy to
Conditional Access and Intune,

10
00:00:31.718 --> 00:00:33.625
targeted by those attributes.

11
00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:38.451
The protocols change, standing Domain
Admin gives way to just-in-time roles,

12
00:00:38.451 --> 00:00:42.887
and management moves to Microsoft
Graph; the slide lays out each pair.

13
00:00:42.887 --> 00:00:45.225
But the key idea is the bottom line.

14
00:00:45.225 --> 00:00:49.462
In Active Directory, governance is
implied by where an object sits.

15
00:00:49.462 --> 00:00:52.677
In Entra ID it has to
be stated explicitly,

16
00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:56.040
as data and rules, or it
simply doesn't exist.
